# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
# Applies to both the pr-gate.yml `trivy fs` scan and the nightly.yml
# container image scans (Trivy reads .trivyignore from the working directory).

# CVE-2026-27456 — util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when setting up loop devices.
# No fixed util-linux version is available yet in the mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0
# base image (Trivy reports no "Fixed Version"). Exploitation requires a local
# unprivileged user plus an /etc/fstab entry using `user,loop` options pointing at an
# attacker-writable path. Our containers run a single non-root app process (USER app)
# with no multi-user shell access and no such fstab entries, so the attack precondition
# does not exist in how these images are deployed.
# Revisit and remove once the base image ships a patched util-linux (>= 2.41.4).
CVE-2026-27456
